---
title: "Keycloak login — proposed (replaces flow-04-login.mmd). Authorization Code + PKCE against Keycloak's own hosted page; the SPA never sees the password. Compare to today: the custom login form posting to /auth/login is gone."
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant SPA as Angular SPA (keycloak-js)
    participant KC as Keycloak (realm ucms)
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant IAM as Identity and Access

    User->>SPA: Open the app
    SPA->>SPA: generate code_verifier + code_challenge (PKCE)
    SPA->>User: redirect browser to Keycloak's hosted login page
    User->>KC: GET /realms/ucms/protocol/openid-connect/auth<br/>...&code_challenge=...
    User->>KC: enter email + password, submit

    KC->>KC: verify password hash<br/>(BCrypt SPI — the hash migrated from identity-access-service, unchanged)
    KC->>KC: check account enabled/disabled (mirrors today's UserStatus)

    alt wrong credentials or disabled
        KC-->>User: login failed, shown on Keycloak's own page
    else credentials valid
        KC-->>User: redirect back to the SPA's redirect_uri with an authorization code
        User->>SPA: lands back on the app
        SPA->>KC: POST /realms/ucms/protocol/openid-connect/token<br/>code + code_verifier
        KC-->>SPA: access_token (RS256 JWT: sub=userId, realm_access.roles),<br/>refresh_token, id_token
        SPA->>GW: GET /api/identity/users/me<br/>Authorization: Bearer access_token
        GW->>KC: validate signature via JWKS (cached)
        GW->>IAM: forward (StripPrefix)
        IAM->>IAM: UcmsJwtAuthenticationConverter → UUID + authorities<br/>(same shape JwtAuthFilter builds today)
        IAM-->>GW: 200 ProfileResponse
        GW-->>SPA: profile
        SPA->>SPA: currentUser signal set, keycloak-js schedules silent refresh
        SPA-->>User: redirected to role dashboard
    end

    Note over SPA,KC: No custom login form, no /auth/login endpoint — Keycloak's own<br/>hosted page collects the password, the SPA and the Gateway never see it.
